+//     the browser theme, and it is what the native frame material is *for*.
+//   * the content panel: the inset rounded card -- the page, the address bar
+//     band above it, and anything else laid out inside it. It wears the page's
+//     own color so the band and the page read as one surface.
+//
+// The material is a property of the window, so every surface-suppressing guard
+// written for it fires window-wide unless it is told otherwise: turning the
+// glass on repainted the band in the app's color, which is the one thing the
+// band must never be. Surfaces inside the card ask this before honouring such
